## Install

LiteArm Studio ships as one self-contained file per platform: no Python, no Node.js and no installer.

* Linux: `litearm-studio-{{version}}-linux-amd64` — verify the `.sha256`, `chmod +x` it, then run it.
* Windows: `litearm-studio-{{version}}-windows-amd64.exe` — verify the `.sha256`, then double-click it.

The Linux file needs glibc 2.35 or newer (Ubuntu 22.04+, Debian 12+). Serial-port permission and
first-run activation are covered in [docs/INSTALL.md]({{@root.host}}/{{@root.owner}}/{{@root.repository}}/blob/{{currentTag}}/docs/INSTALL.md).
